    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nOccupying an enviable position in the heart of picturesque Howth Village, this exceptional architecturally designed residence offers a rare opportunity to acquire a truly distinctive family home. Fully renovated and substantially extended in 2015, with an excellent B rating, the property seamlessly combines contemporary design with practical family living, all within a stone's throw of the village's renowned amenities. Designed to maximise light, space and its enviable surroundings, the home boasts a stunning first-floor open plan living area that serves as the heart of the property. This wonderful space is ideal for modern family life and entertaining, with elevated views that enhance its unique appeal. \n\nAccommodation is generously proportioned and comprises four bedrooms, one ensuite, a fantastic utility area and shower room, all at ground level, while the walnut staircase with sky light leads to the fantastic first floor open plan kitchen and family room with Velux windows, and vaulted ceiling which showcases the views of the beautiful, lush garden to the rear. Glazed doors lead from the kitchen area back into the elegant living/dining room, spanning the width of the property to the front and overlooking Abbey Street below and the ruins of the old Abbey church. At this level there is also a beautifully appointed bathroom with great storage and with original enamel roll-top bath. Altogether a wonderfully thought-out home extending to 173 sq.m. (1,872 sq.ft.) approximately. \nTo the rear lies a spectacular multi-tiered garden, thoughtfully landscaped to create a series of private outdoor spaces for relaxation and entertaining. At ground floor there is a cleverly designed storage shed and steps from here connect to the upper tier levels. The crowning feature is the top decking area, where breathtaking views over Howth Harbour provide the perfect backdrop for enjoying a morning coffee or evening sunset.\n\nThe property has been carefully upgraded to modern standards while respecting its heritage setting. Features include double-glazed windows throughout, with elegant sash windows to the front maintaining the character and charm of the streetscape. Additional benefits include a combi gas boiler, electric vehicle charging point and high-quality finishes throughout.\n\nLocation is simply second to none. Situated in the heart of Howth Village, locals can enjoy an unrivalled selection of cafés, restaurants, shops and local services right on their doorstep. Families will appreciate the proximity to some of North Dublin's most highly regarded primary and secondary schools, while commuters are exceptionally well catered for with a bus service on Abbey Street, the DART station within walking distance and Dublin Airport approximately 17km away. Sporting amenities include sailing, golfing, tennis, football, GAA and rugby amongst many more. Few locations can rival the lifestyle on offer in Howth. This vibrant coastal village combines stunning scenery, excellent amenities and a strong sense of community. From scenic cliff and harbour walks to acclaimed restaurants, cafés and maritime attractions, residents enjoy an exceptional quality of life in one of Dublin's most sought-after coastal settings.\n \nViewing is strictly by appointment only"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nHall - \nTiled hall way and step up into walnut flooring to rear where the staircase is with understairs storage, recessed lights, radiator cover\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.15m x 4.0m\nTo rear, carpet, recessed lights, built-in wardrobes, door to ensuite\n\nEnsuite - 1.0m x 3.55m\nFully tiled, shower, w.c., wash hand basin, recessed lights, heated towel rail, extractor, window\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.25m x 3.25m\nCurrently set up as an office, with desk and storage, TV point, radiator storage press, dimable ceiling strip lighting in addition to recessed lighting, door to garden\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.9m x 3.6m\nTo left of hallway, built-in wardrobe, shelving, recessed lights, walnut flooring\n\nBedroom 4 - 2.4m x 3.6m\nTo right of hallway, built in storage, shelving, walnut flooring\n\nUtility Area - \nExcellent set of storage utility presses plumbed for washing machine and dryer, plus an airing cupboard\n\nShower Room - 1.7m x 2.0m\nFully tiled, shower, w.c., wash hand basin with 2 drawer storage, heated towel rail, recessed lights, window to rear\n\nFirst Floor - \n\n\nKitchen - 4.45m x 4.3m\nLovely bright open-plan kitchen, selection of cream units with granite worktop, integrated 5 ring gas hob, extractor fan, oven, grill and microwave, glazed display cabinets, wine storage, larder press, kitchen island with sink and integrated dishwasher with drop pendant lighting, two sky lights on ceiling and open plan to family room to rear and glazed doors into living room to front\n\nFamily Room - 5.17m x 4.25m\nWonderful relaxing space with vaulted ceiling, Velux windows and views over the fabulous terraced garden to rear, remote controlled gas fire, TV point, built in storage divider, sliding door to outdoor dining decked area and terraced garden beyond\n\nLiving/Dining Room - 7.45m x 3.9m\nOriginal part of the home to the front with three sash windows, gas fireplace with marble surround and original corner decorate open fireplace, walnut flooring, alcove shelving, recessed lights\n\nBathroom - 2.0m x 3.0m\nBehind the kitchen step down to hot press and separate fully tiled bathroom with roll-top enamel bath, w.c., wash hand basin, built-in large storage wardrobe, recessed lights, Velux and window to rear\n\nOutside - \n\n\nFront Garden - \nPaved driveway for two cars\n\nRear Garden - \nMulti-tiered landscaped garden with various seating areas to enjoy outdoor dining and concrete steps leading up to the top level decking where you can enoy fabulous views looking down over Howth Harbour. On the ground level there is artificial grass, raised flower beds and storage shed\n\n"
      },
